+## 2026-11-22, S3 (kids' profiles move to the Box), Sonnet
+Readings of the spec where it was open:
+- `kids.js` already held the cartoon-kid drawing helpers (used by castle-defense); the store is added to the same file, which still has no imports. Name rules are copied from the server (with tests); avatar ids are copied too, and a test keeps them equal to account.js `AVATARS`.
+- **Merge:** the pure functions (`splitProfiles`, `mergeProfiles`, `copyToBox`, `confirmMove`) are in kids.js so they are testable; account.js calls them in one place (`takeProfiles`, used by sign-in and `refresh`). Merged list = grown-ups first, then kids; a kid has `kid: true` (no accountId), and `isKid` checks that flag first. Other code is unchanged.
+- **Grown-up vs kid** on the server = the first profile on an account (by created_at, rowid) is the grown-up's own; the rest are kids. Same rule in the app's split.
+- **`POST /api/profiles`** answers 410 whenever the account already has a profile (always, after sign-up); it still creates one only if an account has none. `/moved` silently skips ids that are not deletable (own, another family's, unknown) and answers with the ids it did delete; History gets one `kids-moved` entry only if N > 0 ("moved N kids' profiles to the Box").
+- The server now also sends `createdAt` on each profile (so the Box keeps their order). `/api/households` gets `kidsWaiting`; the management Families row shows "N kids' profiles waiting to move to the Box" when N > 0.
+- The move deletes on the server only ids read back from the Box store; if the Box can't save (storage error), nothing is sent. A failed call is retried at the next refresh.
+- Backup file import adds only kids whose ids aren't there (never overwrites), respects the 8 limit, skips bad entries and reports counts.
+- Existing server tests that made kids with POST now insert them into the database (`server/test/kids-helper.mjs`); `app/tools/rehearsal-play.mjs` was adjusted the same way (not re-run in full).
+- **Untested / open:** the Tauri save dialog. `saveBackup` uses `window.__TAURI__.dialog.save` + `fs.writeTextFile` if present, otherwise a browser download; the Tauri build has neither plugin yet (only the updater), so in the Windows app it falls back to the browser download, which may not work in the webview. Adding `tauri-plugin-dialog` and `tauri-plugin-fs` (Cargo + capabilities) is needed; I did not touch Rust. Screenshot: `docs/s3/settings-kids-backup.png` (Settings, "Kids" group, shown to signed-in grown-ups only).
+- **S3 review changes (Sonnet):** the move, the safety copies and the restore offer run only when `window.__TAURI_INTERNALS__` exists (`isBoxApp()` in kids.js); elsewhere server kids are shown with `readOnly: true` (no pencil, no Add a child) and nothing is copied or deleted. Rust `app/client/src-tauri/src/backups.rs`: `kids_backup(text) -> path` and `kids_backup_latest()`; files `Documents\Orlis Play\Backups\kids-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.json`, newest 10 kept, only `kids-*.json` ever pruned. The timestamp is **UTC** (no time-zone crate), and two writes in the same minute overwrite. Custom commands need no capability entry in this config. The quiet copy is also written before the server is told (right after the copy), not only after. A "No" to the restore offer is remembered per household (`orlis.kids.declined.<id>`); Load a backup in Settings still works. Screenshot predates this change (Settings buttons unchanged).
